add('lem-type-a-hecke-permutation-modules-have-semistandard-murphy-bases-and-specht-filtrations',[
('one',C,'For the single-box shape and its one-row composition the symmetrizer is the identity and the unique standard tableau is also semistandard. The basis has the lone unit pivot and the ordinary Specht filtration has its sole free quotient; no Garnir violation arises.','Statement tableau basis; Proof1.2 and3.1–4.1'),
('nonempty-choice',C,'Semistandard fibres, Murphy supports and tableau dominance orders are finite. The support-elimination argument and the finite sequence of cell quotients select no arbitrary family, and the final Remarks explicitly state that no choice principle is used.','Proof2.1–4.1; Remarks'),
('iff-forward',NA,'The assertion supplies a basis and a Specht filtration for the specified row permutation module. It does not claim that an arbitrary module possessing such a filtration must be a row permutation module.','Statement basis and filtration; Proof3.1–4.1'),
('iff-reverse',NA,'The generic multiplicity interpretation is an additional conclusion after the universal basis construction. It is not a converse reconstructing a row symmetrizer from multiplicity data or asserting that the generic interpretation characterizes the module over every ring.','Statement generic clause; Proof5.1'),
('degenerate',C,'A singular specialization where the parameter plus the identity vanishes is not excluded. The row-eigenspace proof establishes coordinate identities over the universal domain and then specializes them, explicitly avoiding division by that potentially vanishing scalar. The filtration transfers through the unit-valued permutation pairing over the base ring.','Proof2.1 and4.1'),
('zero',C,'At degree zero the empty composition and empty tableau give the unit row symmetrizer and the base-ring module. Its unique tableau coefficient supplies the unit pivot, and the resulting filtration is the single empty-shape quotient; there are no adjacent generators or Garnir belts. A nonunit Hecke parameter is outside the hypotheses.','Statement unrestricted composition degree; Proof1.2 and3.1–4.1 finite constructions'),
('endpoints',C,'The Garnir straightening process terminates in the finite lexicographic shape and tableau order before using the Murphy dominance refinement. The ensuing finite cell filtration has free quotients, and its reversed star-dual filtration gives the ordinary Specht sections with the same multiplicities.','Statement termination clause; Proof1.2 and4.1')])
