add('thm-schur-functor-images-of-standard-simple-projective-and-tilting-objects',[
('iff-forward',NA,'The theorem computes images of the prescribed standard, simple and projective objects and the tilting flags for the actual tensor Schur functor. It does not give an implication characterizing an arbitrary functor from the occurrence of these image formulas.','Statement numbered conclusions; Proof4.1,6.2–8.1'),
('iff-reverse',NA,'The intrinsic affine-induced Specht identification and the standard-labelled cover recovery are conclusions for the fixed tensor generator. No converse claims that a Specht module or its multiplicities determine a unique ambient category-O object or recover an arbitrary off-standard projective.','Statement clauses1,3,5; Proof5.1 and7.1'),
('one',NA,'Single-column or single-label data are not an extra hypothesis of these image formulas. The proof uses the tensor corner and columnwise affine induction uniformly, and reserves projective recovery for the standard-labelled summands of the detector.','Statement columnwise induction; Proof1.1 and7.1'),
('endpoints',C,'When the column-height bound just reaches the tensor degree, the ordered distinct-row tensor still produces the regular Hecke corner. The proof enlarges to this stable realization and then descends through the supporting-block compression, so the bound is included without a limiting argument.','Proof1.1 and5.1'),
('nonempty-choice',C,'The Statement explicitly assumes the ambient choice axiom for the supplied category-O and Whittaker–Morita machinery. The construction here chooses finitely many terminal boxes after adding finitely many ground rows; its regular-corner and compression maps use those concrete finite data rather than a new arbitrary-index selection.','Statement assumption; Proof1.1 and5.1'),
('zero',C,'Tensor degree zero has the empty tensor word, the identity permutation and no dot exponents in the stable-corner construction. The associated empty column partitions induce the ground standard image; the projective-summand evaluation and exact image formulas retain these degree-zero objects.','Statement tensor generator unrestricted degree; Proof1.1 and7.1'),
('degenerate',C,'A pyramid below the distinct-row stable bound is not excluded. Full ground rows are added without changing the column partitions or affine roots, and the zero-deleted-occupancy supporting-block compression identifies the original standard image with the large realization.','Proof1.1 and5.1')])
